# Design-catalogue visual baselines. Ubuntu is the authoritative renderer (CI
# runs ubuntu-24.04), so only the linux set is tracked. LFS keeps each baseline
# version pinned to its commit while git history stores pointer files — the
# concern is not the initial ~70 MB but that every regenerated PNG would
# otherwise add a full, undeltifiable blob to a 1.7 GB object database forever.
e2e/ui/visual-catalog.test.ts-snapshots/*-linux.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
